ggregate comparison tables to show how LoRA-only performs against the SDF variants across different lambda values and seeds. Generating markdown table...\n\nNow I'm noticing the Phase 2 results show an interesting trade-off—TSR improves significantly from 6% to 16.5% when we remove the SDF loss after 10K steps, though it still lags behind the baseline. I need to verify the LoRA baseline evaluation details before finalizing the YAML output, since those results should already be in the registry. results stand. So I should present them as-is but note they're confirmed data.\n\nBut actually, the median tier specification says the existing LoRA 2-seed results ARE the \"confirmed\" starting point (CAR=55.3%, TSR=6.3% from paper_framing). The median tier's departure from reality is mainly:\n1. LoRA seed2 comes in lower (48%) → 3-seed mean drops to 52.8%\n2. Phase 2 shows weak persistence\n3. Lambda=0.1 shows weak dose-response\n4. spatial_bowl can't be attributed without LoRA control\n\nSo plan_003 results are real data, not imagined. Let me note that.\n\nFor plan_004 (LoRA training, DONE): also real data.\n\nNow I'm checking the expected TSR values across the different seeds and conditions to make sure they're internally consistent before writing the YAML. Writing YAML output...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7481,"cache_read_input_tokens":35822,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7481},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"817f4f38-eb3e-4426-9c0e-6fb4c2501da3","uuid":"071f801f-3dd3-47b6-8969-ccfb15c65db8"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_015WE7VmxE24t8e651GDixKG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the experiment plan, registry data, and the median tier specification, I'll generate detailed predictions for all active experiments.\n\n```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: |\n  Claim 4 从 \"SDF is redundant\" 降级为 \"SDF is largely redundant at typical lambda\n  (≤0.01); extreme lambda (0.1) shows marginal, statistically ambiguous CAR benefit\n  (~+6pp) that does not justify added complexity.\" Phase 2 弱持久性信号需承认但 frame\n  为 \"weak and practically insignificant — TSR remains collapsed at 16.5%.\"\n  LoRA seed2 拉低 3-seed 均值至 52.8%，3v3 one-sided p=0.24，无法 claim \"statistically\n  indistinguishable\" 但差异无实际意义。论文叙事从 \"clean negative\" 变为 \"predominantly\n  negative with boundary conditions.\" Claims 1-3 不受影响。dfCAR threshold 在\n  δ∈[2mm,200mm] 完全稳定。spatial_bowl 缺少 LoRA control 无法做跨场景 SDF 归因。\n  CoRL 估算 45-55%。需补充一段 discussion 解释 lambda dose-response 的 ceiling\n  和 practical implications。Claim 4 措辞加 hedging: \"largely redundant\" /\n  \"provides no practically significant benefit at standard hyperparameter ranges.\"\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_003: LoRA baseline eval (2 seeds) — CONFIRMED DATA\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"LoRA baseline eval (2 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_003\"\n    description: \"LoRA-only (无 SDF) 30K checkpoint eval, 2 seeds × 200 episodes\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_avg_CAR: 54.5\n      seed0_avg_TSR: 8.5\n      seed0_avg_ee_disp: 0.489\n      seed0_frozen_pct: 0\n      seed1_avg_CAR: 56.0\n      seed1_avg_TSR: 4.0\n      seed1_avg_ee_disp: 0.467\n      seed1_frozen_pct: 0\n      two_seed_mean_CAR: 55.25\n      two_seed_mean_TSR: 6.25\n      dfCAR_100mm: 55.25\n      fake_safety: false\n    result_rationale: |\n      已确认数据。LoRA fine-tuning on collision-free demonstrations 产生真实碰撞避免:\n      EE displacement ~0.48m 证实机器人正常运动 (非 action collapse), frozen_pct=0%,\n      dfCAR = raw CAR (无 filtering)。CAR=55% 代表 +29pp vs Pi0.5 baseline (27%),\n      完全来自隐式 demo 信号而非几何监督。TSR 从 73% 坍缩至 6.25% 是 catastrophic\n      forgetting 的结果——模型学会了保守行为 (conservative avoidance) 而非真正的安全\n      感知 (safety awareness)。两个 seed 间 CAR 差异 1.5pp 在评估噪声范围内。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"LoRA-only Per-Task Breakdown (2 seeds)\"\n        columns: [\"Task\", \"s0 CAR\", \"s0 TSR\", \"s0 EE Disp\", \"s1 CAR\", \"s1 TSR\", \"s1 EE Disp\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"orange_juice\", \"62\", \"0\", \"0.497\", \"58\", \"2\", \"0.483\"]\n          - [\"chocolate_pudding\", \"44\", \"34\", \"0.504\", \"50\", \"14\", \"0.538\"]\n          - [\"milk\", \"94\", \"0\", \"0.577\", \"90\", \"0\", \"0.482\"]\n          - [\"bbq_sauce\", \"18\", \"0\", \"0.377\", \"26\", \"0\", \"0.365\"]\n          - [\"Mean\", \"54.5\", \"8.5\", \"0.489\", \"56.0\", \"4.0\", \"0.467\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: 4-task CAR for LoRA s0 vs s1, 展示 per-task pattern 一致性 (milk 最高, bbq_sauce 最低)\"\n    analysis: |\n      LoRA-only 已建立真实避障 baseline: CAR=55%, 0% fake safety, EE disp ~0.48m。\n      Per-task pattern 由任务布局决定 (milk 障碍物位置有利, bbq_sauce 障碍物遮挡严重),\n      这一 pattern 在 SDF 模型中完全复制——进一步说明 CAR 来源是 demo imitation 而非\n      geometric supervision。2-seed 数据足以建立 baseline, 但 3v3 统计对比需 seed2。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_005: Phase 2 λ=0 training (seed2)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Phase 2 lambda=0 training (seed2)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_005\"\n    description: \"从 train_pi05_a1_obj_s2_l005 的 10K SDF checkpoint resume, λ=0 训练至 30K\"\n    expected_results:\n      final_loss: 0.0118\n      best_loss: 0.0089\n      best_step: 22000\n      total_steps: 30000\n      grad_norm: 0.112\n      time_per_step: 4.6\n      training_stable: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      Phase 2 从已有 SDF imprint 的 10K checkpoint 出发, 移除 SDF loss (λ=0) 继续训练\n      20K 步。loss 从 ~0.015 (10K SDF 的 total_loss) 下降到 ~0.012, 因为移除 SDF\n      auxiliary loss 后模型只需优化 action loss, 训练变得更容易。但 loss 不会降到\n      LoRA-only 水平 (0.010) 因为 10K 步 SDF 训练已改变了模型的 representation\n      landscape, 后续优化在不同的 basin 中进行。best_loss 出现在 22K 步 (即 Phase 2\n      的 12K 步处), 之后因缺乏 demo 多样性而轻微过拟合。训练稳定, 无 NaN 或梯度爆炸。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: |\n      训练成功完成。loss 轨迹确认 SDF removal 后模型能正常优化, 但 loss 轨迹\n      与 LoRA-only 不同, 暗示 SDF 训练确实改变了 model 的 loss landscape。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_006: Phase 2 λ=0 eval (seed2)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Phase 2 lambda=0 eval (seed2)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: \"Phase 2 训练完成后 eval, 200 episodes, 提取 TSR/CAR/EE displacement\"\n    expected_results:\n      avg_CAR: 61\n      avg_TSR: 18\n      n_episodes: 200\n      avg_ee_disp: 0.462\n      frozen_pct: 0\n      dfCAR_100mm: 61\n      task0_CAR: 68\n      task0_TSR: 10\n      task0_ee_disp: 0.478\n      task1_CAR: 48\n      task1_TSR: 48\n      task1_ee_disp: 0.502\n      task2_CAR: 86\n      task2_TSR: 2\n      task2_ee_disp: 0.542\n      task3_CAR: 42\n      task3_TSR: 12\n      task3_ee_disp: 0.326\n    result_rationale: |\n      Phase 2 CAR=61% 高于 LoRA-only (55%) 和 SDF 30K (50.5%), 暗示 SDF 留下了弱\n      持久效应。机制解释: 10K 步 SDF 训练在模型 intermediate representations 中\n      编码了微弱的几何距离感知, 当 SDF loss 移除后, 这些 representations 部分保留\n      (不被后续训练完全覆盖), 产生略高的碰撞避免率。\n      \n      但这个 +6pp 效应在统计上模糊: 单 seed 评估的 eval noise 约 ±3-5pp (参见\n      s0 λ=0.005 两次评估差 3pp)。需要 plan_012 的第二个 Phase 2 seed 确认。\n      \n      TSR=18% 部分恢复 (vs SDF 30K 的 ~7% 和 baseline 的 73%): 移除 SDF loss\n      允许模型在后续 20K 步中部分重新学习 task completion, 但起始点 (10K SDF\n      checkpoint) 已经严重偏离 task-optimal trajectory, 恢复有限。task1 (chocolate_pudding)\n      恢复最好 (TSR=48%) 因为该任务最 \"可学\" (baseline TSR=86%); task2 (milk)\n      几乎不恢复 (TSR=2%) 因为其 CAR 已经很高 (86%), 模型选择保持保守。\n      \n      关键: 即使 Phase 2 CAR 偏高, TSR=18% 仍远低于实用要求, 说明 two-phase strategy\n      (先学 safety → 再恢复 task) 在当前训练量和 LoRA 配置下不可行。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Phase 2 vs LoRA-only vs SDF 30K 对比\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"CAR (%)\", \"TSR (%)\", \"EE Disp (m)\", \"Fake Safe\", \"Seeds\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Pi0.5 baseline\", \"27.0\", \"74.7\", \"0.15\", \"98.2%\", \"3\"]\n          - [\"LoRA-only 30K\", \"52.8\", \"5.8\", \"0.48\", \"0%\", \"3*\"]\n          - [\"SDF lambda=0.005 30K\", \"50.5\", \"6.8\", \"0.48\", \"0%\", \"3\"]\n          - [\"SDF lambda=0.01 30K\", \"52.7\", \"7.0\", \"0.48\", \"0%\", \"3\"]\n          - [\"Phase 2 (10K SDF -> 20K lambda=0)\", \"61.0\", \"18.0\", \"0.46\", \"0%\", \"1\"]\n      - name: \"Phase 2 Per-Task Breakdown (seed2)\"\n        columns: [\"Task\", \"CAR (%)\", \"TSR (%)\", \"EE Disp (m)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"orange_juice\", \"68\", \"10\", \"0.478\"]\n          - [\"chocolate_pudding\", \"48\", \"48\", \"0.502\"]\n          - [\"milk\", \"86\", \"2\", \"0.542\"]\n          - [\"bbq_sauce\", \"42\", \"12\", \"0.326\"]\n          - [\"Mean\", \"61\", \"18\", \"0.462\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: CAR/TSR for LoRA-only vs SDF 30K vs Phase 2, 显示 Phase 2 的 CAR 略高但 TSR 仍坍缩\"\n      - \"Per-task scatter: Phase 2 per-task CAR vs LoRA-only per-task CAR, 预期 Phase 2 全面略高但保持同样的 task ordering\"\n    analysis: |\n      Phase 2 呈现弱 persistence 信号: CAR 比 LoRA-only 高 ~6pp, TSR 部分恢复至 18%。\n      但单 seed 不足以做统计推断。这个结果需要 hedging: \"Phase 2 shows a trend toward\n      weak SDF persistence, but with n=1 and evaluation noise of ±5pp, the effect is\n      not statistically reliable.\" TSR=18% 远低于 baseline 73%, 说明 two-phase strategy\n      在当前配置下不具实用性。论文中应放在 discussion 而非 main results。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_007: spatial_bowl A1 training (seed0, λ=0.005)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"spatial_bowl A1 SDF training\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_007\"\n    description: \"Pi0.5 + LoRA + SDF (λ=0.005) on spatial_bowl scene, seed0, 30K steps\"\n    expected_results:\n      final_loss: 0.0152\n      best_loss: 0.0128\n      best_step: 20000\n      total_steps: 30000\n      grad_norm: 0.18\n      time_per_step: 4.8\n      training_stable: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      spatial_bowl 场景的 loss 高于 object_pudding (0.013 vs 0.008) 因为: (1) spatial\n      tasks 涉及更复杂的操作路径 (在 plate/ramekin 间取碗), action 预测难度更高;\n      (2) SDF loss 在 spatial 场景中贡献更大 (更多 close-proximity 情况), 推高\n      total loss。训练稳定, 无异常。best_loss 出现在 20K 步而非 26K, 因为 spatial\n      场景的 SDF loss 使训练曲线更不稳定, 过拟合更早出现。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: |\n      训练成功完成。spatial_bowl 训练的 loss 比 object_pudding 高约 60%, 反映场景\n      复杂度差异。跨场景 SDF 效果归因需要 plan_015 (LoRA-only control) 完成,\n      但在 median tier 下 plan_015 不会在 deadline 前完成。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_008: spatial_bowl eval\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"spatial_bowl SDF eval\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_008\"\n    description: \"spatial_bowl A1 训练完成后 eval, 200 episodes, 验证跨场景 CAR/TSR pattern\"\n    expected_results:\n      avg_CAR: 35\n      avg_TSR: 3\n      n_episodes: 200\n      avg_ee_disp: 0.248\n      frozen_pct: 0\n      fake_safety: false\n      task0_CAR: 38\n      task0_TSR: 4\n      task0_ee_disp: 0.263\n      task1_CAR: 28\n      task1_TSR: 0\n      task1_ee_disp: 0.231\n      task2_CAR: 48\n      task2_TSR: 6\n      task2_ee_disp: 0.274\n      task3_CAR: 26\n      task3_TSR: 2\n      task3_ee_disp: 0.224\n    result_rationale: |\n      spatial_bowl SDF CAR=35% 显著低于 object_pudding SDF (50.5%), 原因:\n      (1) spatial_bowl 任务布局更紧凑——碗被 plate/ramekin/stove 环绕, 机械臂\n      几乎不可能在不碰触障碍物的情况下完成 pick 动作; (2) 碰撞类型以 arm-body\n      为主 (EE-only SDF 无法防护); (3) 障碍物体积更大且更密集。\n      \n      EE displacement ~0.25m 低于 object_pudding (0.48m) 因为 spatial tasks 的\n      操作空间更小, 机械臂运动范围受限。fake_safety=0% 确认 SDF LoRA 在\n      spatial_bowl 也产生真实运动。\n      \n      task2 (pick_bowl_on_stove) CAR 最高 (48%) 因为 stove 上方空间较大,\n      碰撞风险较低; task3 (pick_bowl_on_cabinet) CAR 最低 (26%) 因为 cabinet\n      两侧有遮挡。TSR=3% 极低, 与 object_pudding 的 TSR=7% 一致——都是\n      catastrophic forgetting, spatial 更严重因为任务本身更难 (baseline TSR=57.5%)。\n      \n      关键限制: 没有 spatial_bowl LoRA-only control (plan_015), 无法判断这\n      35% CAR 是 SDF 贡献还是 LoRA-only 就能达到。如果 spatial LoRA-only\n      CAR 也 ~35%, 则进一步确认 SDF 冗余; 如果 CAR ~26% (接近 baseline),\n      则 SDF 可能在 spatial 场景有 +9pp 效应——但无法验证。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"spatial_bowl Per-Task Breakdown\"\n        columns: [\"Task\", \"CAR (%)\", \"TSR (%)\", \"EE Disp (m)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"bowl_between_plate_ramekin\", \"38\", \"4\", \"0.263\"]\n          - [\"bowl_on_ramekin\", \"28\", \"0\", \"0.231\"]\n          - [\"bowl_on_stove\", \"48\", \"6\", \"0.274\"]\n          - [\"bowl_on_cabinet\", \"26\", \"2\", \"0.224\"]\n          - [\"Mean\", \"35\", \"3\", \"0.248\"]\n      - name: \"跨场景对比 (SDF lambda=0.005)\"\n        columns: [\"Scene\", \"CAR (%)\", \"TSR (%)\", \"EE Disp (m)\", \"LoRA Control?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"object_pudding\", \"50.5\", \"6.8\", \"0.48\", \"Yes (3 seeds)\"]\n          - [\"spatial_bowl\", \"35\", \"3\", \"0.25\", \"No\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Side-by-side per-task CAR bar chart: object_pudding vs spatial_bowl, 展示 CAR 在 spatial 场景系统性下降\"\n    analysis: |\n      spatial_bowl 数据展示 SDF+LoRA 的跨场景泛化, 但因缺少 LoRA-only control\n      (plan_015), 无法做 SDF 归因。在论文中只能呈现为 \"SDF+LoRA in spatial_bowl\n      achieves 35% CAR with 0% fake safety\" 而不能说 \"SDF contributes Xpp.\"\n      这是 median tier 的关键 gap: 跨场景 SDF attribution 缺失。\n      建议: 论文放在 appendix 作为跨场景泛化的 preliminary observation, 而非\n      main claim 的 evidence。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_009: Lambda=0.1 bracket training (2 seeds)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Lambda=0.1 bracket training (2 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_009\"\n    description: \"Pi0.5 + LoRA + SDF (λ=0.1) on object_pudding, s0+s1, 30K steps each\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_final_loss: 0.0385\n      seed0_best_loss: 0.0312\n      seed0_best_step: 16000\n      seed1_final_loss: 0.0371\n      seed1_best_loss: 0.0298\n      seed1_best_step: 18000\n      total_steps: 30000\n      training_stable: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      λ=0.1 的 total loss 显著高于 λ=0.005/0.01 (0.038 vs 0.014) 因为 SDF\n      auxiliary loss 在高 lambda 下成为 dominant loss component。action_loss 本身\n      可能只有 ~0.012, 但 SDF loss × 0.1 贡献 ~0.025, 使 total loss 翻倍。\n      best_loss 出现在 16-18K 步 (比 λ=0.005 的 10-26K 更早), 因为高 lambda\n      使训练更不稳定, 过拟合/振荡更早出现。两个 seed 的 loss 轨迹相似,\n      seed1 略好因为随机初始化差异。训练稳定, 无梯度爆炸。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: |\n      训练完成但 loss 明显高于低 lambda 配置。高 SDF penalty 压制了 action loss\n      优化, 预期 eval 时 TSR 进一步下降。这是 \"dose-response\" 的训练侧信号:\n      更强的几何约束 = 更高的 total loss = 更大的 task 性能牺牲。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_010: Lambda=0.1 eval\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Lambda=0.1 eval (2 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010\"\n    description: \"Lambda=0.1 训练完成后 eval, 验证 lambda 递增是否 monotonic 提升 CAR\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_avg_CAR: 57\n      seed0_avg_TSR: 4\n      seed0_ee_disp: 0.445\n      seed1_avg_CAR: 60\n      seed1_avg_TSR: 4\n      seed1_ee_disp: 0.458\n      two_seed_mean_CAR: 58.5\n      two_seed_mean_TSR: 4.0\n      seed0_task0_CAR: 72\n      seed0_task0_TSR: 0\n      seed0_task1_CAR: 46\n      seed0_task1_TSR: 16\n      seed0_task2_CAR: 90\n      seed0_task2_TSR: 0\n      seed0_task3_CAR: 20\n      seed0_task3_TSR: 0\n      seed1_task0_CAR: 70\n      seed1_task0_TSR: 2\n      seed1_task1_CAR: 50\n      seed1_task1_TSR: 14\n      seed1_task2_CAR: 92\n      seed1_task2_TSR: 0\n      seed1_task3_CAR: 28\n      seed1_task3_TSR: 0\n      lambda_curve_slope_pp_per_001lambda: 0.75\n      frozen_pct: 0\n    result_rationale: |\n      Lambda=0.1 CAR=58.5% 高于 λ=0.005 (50.5%) 和 λ=0.01 (52.7%), 呈现弱\n      dose-response: 20× lambda 增幅 → +6pp CAR。机制: 更高的 SDF penalty 迫使\n      模型在训练中更强地回避障碍物区域, 产生更保守的 action distribution。\n      \n      但这个 dose-response 是 sublinear 的: λ 从 0.005→0.01 (2×) 只带来 +2pp;\n      λ 从 0.01→0.1 (10×) 带来 +6pp。边际收益递减。且 TSR 从 ~7% 下降到 4%,\n      说明更高的 CAR 以更多 task 性能为代价。\n      \n      Per-task pattern 保持一致 (milk 最高, bbq_sauce 最低), 说明 CAR 分布\n      仍由任务布局主导而非 SDF 强度。task0 (orange_juice) CAR 从 ~60%→70%\n      提升最大, 可能因为该任务的障碍物位置恰好在 SDF gradient 能有效作用的区域。\n      \n      统计上: 2-seed 的 SE ≈ 2.1pp, 与 LoRA 3-seed mean (52.8%) 的差异\n      = 58.5 - 52.8 = 5.7pp, t ≈ 1.2, p ≈ 0.15 (one-sided)。在 [0.1, 0.3]\n      范围内——有 trend 但不显著。这正是 median tier 的 \"弱信号\": 无法断言\n      SDF 在高 lambda 下完全无效, 但效应边缘且代价 (TSR 进一步下降) 使其\n      实际无意义。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"4-Point Lambda Dose-Response Curve\"\n        columns: [\"Lambda\", \"CAR Mean (%)\", \"CAR SD\", \"TSR Mean (%)\", \"n_seeds\", \"Delta vs LoRA\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"0 (LoRA-only)\", \"52.8\", \"4.2\", \"5.8\", \"3\", \"ref\"]\n          - [\"0.005\", \"50.5\", \"3.0\", \"6.8\", \"3\", \"-2.3\"]\n          - [\"0.01\", \"52.7\", \"0.3\", \"7.0\", \"3\", \"-0.1\"]\n          - [\"0.1\", \"58.5\", \"2.1\", \"4.0\", \"2\", \"+5.7\"]\n      - name: \"Lambda=0.1 Per-Task Breakdown (2 seeds)\"\n        columns: [\"Task\", \"s0 CAR\", \"s0 TSR\", \"s1 CAR\", \"s1 TSR\", \"Mean CAR\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"orange_juice\", \"72\", \"0\", \"70\", \"2\", \"71\"]\n          - [\"chocolate_pudding\", \"46\", \"16\", \"50\", \"14\", \"48\"]\n          - [\"milk\", \"90\", \"0\", \"92\", \"0\", \"91\"]\n          - [\"bbq_sauce\", \"20\", \"0\", \"28\", \"0\", \"24\"]\n          - [\"Mean\", \"57\", \"4\", \"60\", \"4\", \"58.5\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Lambda-CAR curve: x-axis = lambda (log scale, 0.005-0.1), y-axis = CAR (%). 含 LoRA baseline 水平虚线 (52.8%). 展示非线性 dose-response, λ=0.1 处斜率开始上翘但仍在 LoRA±SE 范围内\"\n      - \"Lambda-TSR curve: 同 x-axis, y-axis = TSR (%). 展示 TSR 随 lambda 递减的趋势 (7% → 4%), 说明 CAR gain 以 TSR loss 为代价\"\n      - \"CAR-TSR tradeoff scatter (Fig 5 候选): 每个 lambda 点画一个点, 连线展示 pareto frontier 方向\"\n    analysis: |\n      Lambda dose-response 存在但很弱: regression slope = 0.75 pp/0.01λ (在 [0.5, 2.0]\n      范围内)。关键 insight: SDF geometric supervision 在极端 lambda 下能\"挤出\"\n      额外 ~6pp CAR, 但 (1) 效果不显著 (p=0.15), (2) 代价是 TSR 进一步下降,\n      (3) 收益有 ceiling (已有 53% 来自 demo imitation, SDF 只加 6pp)。\n      \n      论文写法: \"Increasing λ from 0.01 to 0.1 yields a modest CAR increase\n      (+6pp), suggesting SDF geometric supervision can provide marginal benefit\n      at extreme penalty weights. However, this improvement is not statistically\n      significant (p=0.15, 2-seed) and comes at the cost of further task\n      performance degradation (TSR: 7%→4%). The practical value of this\n      tradeoff is negligible.\"\n      \n      需要 discussion 段解释 lambda ceiling: 为什么 10× lambda 只换来 6pp?\n      可能原因: (1) EE-only SDF 的 structural limitation (arm-body 碰撞不被覆盖);\n      (2) demo signal 已经 capture 了大部分可学的 avoidance behavior;\n      (3) 更高 lambda 主要 suppress 运动而非改进轨迹。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_012: Phase 2 additional seed (seed0)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Phase 2 lambda=0 additional seed (seed0)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: \"从 s0 的 10K SDF checkpoint resume with λ=0, 训练至 30K, 然后 eval\"\n    expected_results:\n      training_final_loss: 0.0124\n      training_best_loss: 0.0092\n      eval_avg_CAR: 58\n      eval_avg_TSR: 15\n      eval_n_episodes: 200\n      eval_avg_ee_disp: 0.455\n      eval_frozen_pct: 0\n      eval_task0_CAR: 66\n      eval_task0_TSR: 6\n      eval_task1_CAR: 46\n      eval_task1_TSR: 40\n      eval_task2_CAR: 82\n      eval_task2_TSR: 0\n      eval_task3_CAR: 38\n      eval_task3_TSR: 14\n      phase2_2seed_mean_CAR: 59.5\n      phase2_2seed_mean_TSR: 16.5\n      phase2_vs_lora_delta: 6.7\n    result_rationale: |\n      Phase 2 seed0 CAR=58% 与 seed2 (61%) 一致但略低, 展示 Phase 2 结果的\n      seed-to-seed variance (~3pp)。两个 Phase 2 seed 的均值 = 59.5%, 比\n      LoRA-only (52.8%) 高 6.7pp。\n      \n      这个 delta 与 Lambda=0.1 的 delta (+5.7pp) 处于同一量级, 暗示两种路径\n      (持久效应 vs 强 penalty) 达到相似的 marginal effect ceiling。但 Phase 2\n      的 TSR 恢复更好 (16.5% vs 4%), 因为 Phase 2 在 λ=0 阶段有机会重新\n      优化 task completion, 而 λ=0.1 始终被高 SDF penalty 压制。\n      \n      关键: 2-seed Phase 2 的 within-condition variance (SD ≈ 2pp) 比 LoRA\n      3-seed variance (SD = 4.2pp) 小, 但因为 n=2 的自由度极低, 统计功效\n      不足以做可靠推断。Phase 2 vs LoRA 的 t-test 给出 p ≈ 0.12 (one-sided),\n      在 [0.1, 0.3] 边界——suggestive but not conclusive。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Phase 2 Multi-Seed Summary\"\n        columns: [\"Phase 2 Seed\", \"CAR (%)\", \"TSR (%)\", \"EE Disp (m)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"seed2 (from s2 10K ckpt)\", \"61\", \"18\", \"0.462\"]\n          - [\"seed0 (from s0 10K ckpt)\", \"58\", \"15\", \"0.455\"]\n          - [\"Mean\", \"59.5\", \"16.5\", \"0.459\"]\n      - name: \"Phase 2 Persistence Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"CAR (%)\", \"TSR (%)\", \"Delta CAR vs LoRA\", \"p (one-sided)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LoRA-only (3 seeds)\", \"52.8\", \"5.8\", \"ref\", \"ref\"]\n          - [\"SDF lambda=0.005 30K (3 seeds)\", \"50.5\", \"6.8\", \"-2.3\", \"0.24\"]\n          - [\"SDF lambda=0.01 30K (3 seeds)\", \"52.7\", \"7.0\", \"-0.1\", \"0.48\"]\n          - [\"Phase 2 (2 seeds)\", \"59.5\", \"16.5\", \"+6.7\", \"0.12\"]\n          - [\"Lambda=0.1 (2 seeds)\", \"58.5\", \"4.0\", \"+5.7\", \"0.15\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: 5 conditions (LoRA, SDF 0.005, SDF 0.01, Phase 2, Lambda=0.1) 的 CAR/TSR side-by-side, 展示 Phase 2 和 Lambda=0.1 的 marginal CAR gain 但 TSR 仍坍缩\"\n    analysis: |\n      Phase 2 的 2-seed 均值 (59.5%) 确认弱持久效应。但效应量 (~7pp) 在\n      eval noise 范围内 (单次 eval ±3-5pp), 且 n=2 功效不足。\n      \n      论文写法: \"Phase 2 training (removing SDF loss after 10K steps) shows\n      a trend toward higher CAR (59.5% vs 52.8% for LoRA-only, p=0.12),\n      suggesting SDF training may leave a weak persistent imprint. However,\n      task performance remains heavily degraded (TSR=16.5% vs 73% baseline),\n      and the effect size is within the range of evaluation noise. We interpret\n      this as weak evidence of SDF persistence that does not alter our primary\n      conclusion: SDF geometric supervision provides no practically significant\n      benefit.\"\n      \n      Phase 2 需放在 discussion 中, 不能作为 Claim 4 的反例。Frame 为\n      \"boundary condition\" and \"future investigation direction.\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_013: LoRA baseline seed2\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"LoRA baseline seed2 (training + eval)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_013\"\n    description: \"第三个 LoRA-only seed, 使 SDF 归因对比有 3v3 seeds\"\n    expected_results:\n      training_final_loss: 0.0142\n      training_best_loss: 0.0112\n      training_best_step: 18000\n      training_total_steps: 30000\n      eval_avg_CAR: 48\n      eval_avg_TSR: 5\n      eval_n_episodes: 200\n      eval_avg_ee_disp: 0.458\n      eval_frozen_pct: 0\n      eval_dfCAR_100mm: 48\n      eval_task0_CAR: 54\n      eval_task0_TSR: 0\n      eval_task0_ee_disp: 0.472\n      eval_task1_CAR: 38\n      eval_task1_TSR: 18\n      eval_task1_ee_disp: 0.497\n      eval_task2_CAR: 78\n      eval_task2_TSR: 0\n      eval_task2_ee_disp: 0.521\n      eval_task3_CAR: 22\n      eval_task3_TSR: 2\n      eval_task3_ee_disp: 0.343\n      lora_3seed_mean_CAR: 52.8\n      lora_3seed_sd_CAR: 4.2\n      sdf_delta_l005_vs_lora: -2.3\n      sdf_delta_l01_vs_lora: -0.1\n      welch_t_l005: 0.78\n      welch_p_l005_onesided: 0.24\n      welch_t_l01: 0.07\n      welch_p_l01_onesided: 0.48\n    result_rationale: |\n      LoRA seed2 CAR=48% 低于 s0 (54.5%) 和 s1 (56%), 将 3-seed 均值拉低至\n      52.8%。这个 seed-to-seed 差异 (48-56%, range=8pp) 反映 LoRA fine-tuning\n      的随机性: 不同的 LoRA adapter 初始化导致模型收敛到不同的 local optima,\n      有些 optima 更 \"保守\" (高 CAR, 低 TSR), 有些更 \"积极\" (低 CAR, 高 TSR)。\n      \n      具体到 seed2: task2 (milk) CAR=78% 明显低于 s0/s1 的 90-94%, 这是主要\n      的差异来源。milk 任务在不同 seed 间的 CAR 变化大, 可能因为该任务的\n      obstacle 位置恰好在 action distribution 的边界——微小的 policy 差异就能\n      导致 \"刚好碰到\" vs \"刚好避开\"。\n      \n      3v3 统计对比:\n      - vs SDF λ=0.005: delta = -2.3pp, t=0.78, p=0.24 (one-sided)\n        解读: LoRA 可能略优于 SDF, 但 p=0.24 不足以 reject \"无差异\" null\n      - vs SDF λ=0.01: delta = -0.1pp, t=0.07, p=0.48\n        解读: 几乎完全相同\n      \n      关键: 高 variance (SD=4.2pp) 来自 LoRA seed2 的异常值。SDF 3-seed 的\n      variance 更小 (λ=0.005: SD=3.0, λ=0.01: SD=0.3), 说明 SDF loss 可能\n      有 regularization 效应——压缩 seed-to-seed variance。但这不构成 \"SDF\n      is useful\" 的 argument, 因为 variance reduction 不等于 performance gain。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"3v3 LoRA vs SDF Seed-Level Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"Seed 0\", \"Seed 1\", \"Seed 2\", \"Mean\", \"SD\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LoRA-only CAR (%)\", \"54.5\", \"56.0\", \"48.0\", \"52.8\", \"4.2\"]\n          - [\"LoRA-only TSR (%)\", \"8.5\", \"4.0\", \"5.0\", \"5.8\", \"2.3\"]\n          - [\"SDF l=0.005 CAR (%)\", \"47.0\", \"51.5\", \"53.0\", \"50.5\", \"3.0\"]\n          - [\"SDF l=0.005 TSR (%)\", \"7.5\", \"4.0\", \"9.0\", \"6.8\", \"2.5\"]\n          - [\"SDF l=0.01 CAR (%)\", \"52.5\", \"52.5\", \"53.0\", \"52.7\", \"0.3\"]\n          - [\"SDF l=0.01 TSR (%)\", \"6.5\", \"7.5\", \"7.5\", \"7.2\", \"0.6\"]\n      - name: \"3v3 Statistical Tests (CAR)\"\n        columns: [\"Comparison\", \"Delta (pp)\", \"Welch t\", \"p (one-sided)\", \"Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LoRA vs SDF l=0.005\", \"-2.3\", \"0.78\", \"0.24\", \"trend, not significant\"]\n          - [\"LoRA vs SDF l=0.01\", \"-0.1\", \"0.07\", \"0.48\", \"no difference\"]\n      - name: \"LoRA seed2 Per-Task Breakdown\"\n        columns: [\"Task\", \"CAR (%)\", \"TSR (%)\", \"EE Disp (m)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"orange_juice\", \"54\", \"0\", \"0.472\"]\n          - [\"chocolate_pudding\", \"38\", \"18\", \"0.497\"]\n          - [\"milk\", \"78\", \"0\", \"0.521\"]\n          - [\"bbq_sauce\", \"22\", \"2\", \"0.343\"]\n          - [\"Mean\", \"48\", \"5\", \"0.458\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Box plot: 3 LoRA seeds vs 3 SDF seeds (l=0.005 和 l=0.01), 展示 distributions 高度重叠, LoRA 有更大 spread\"\n      - \"Per-task line plot: 4 tasks × 6 conditions (3 LoRA + 3 SDF), 展示 per-task ordering 完全一致 (milk > orange_juice > chocolate_pudding > bbq_sauce)\"\n    analysis: |\n      LoRA seed2 引入的 variance 使 3v3 对比从 \"clearly indistinguishable\" 变为\n      \"not statistically distinguishable but with a suggestive trend.\" p=0.24\n      (one-sided) 落在论文写作的 awkward zone: 不能 claim \"SDF = LoRA\"\n      (需 equivalence test, 但 n=3 功效不足), 也不能 claim \"SDF < LoRA\"\n      (p > 0.1)。\n      \n      论文措辞需从 D025 的 \"SDF delta = 0pp\" 调整为:\n      \"The mean CAR difference between LoRA-only (52.8±4.2%) and SDF\n      (50.5±3.0% at λ=0.005; 52.7±0.3% at λ=0.01) is not statistically\n      significant (p=0.24 and p=0.48, respectively, one-sided Welch t-test).\n      We cannot formally claim equivalence with n=3 seeds, but the effect\n      size (≤2.3pp) is well within evaluation noise and below any threshold\n      of practical significance.\"\n      \n      这比 \"SDF is redundant\" 弱, 但仍支持 \"SDF provides no practically\n      significant benefit\" 的 hedged claim。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_014: dfCAR threshold sensitivity analysis\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"dfCAR threshold sensitivity analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_014\"\n    description: \"CPU-only 分析: 在 delta={2mm,5mm,10mm,20mm,50mm,100mm} 上计算 dfCAR\"\n    expected_results:\n      a1_pi0_raw_CAR: 91.5\n      a1_pi0_dfCAR_2mm: 0.4\n      a1_pi0_dfCAR_5mm: 0.4\n      a1_pi0_dfCAR_10mm: 0.4\n      a1_pi0_dfCAR_20mm: 0\n      a1_pi0_dfCAR_50mm: 0\n      a1_pi0_dfCAR_100mm: 0\n      lora_only_raw_CAR: 52.8\n      lora_only_dfCAR_all_thresholds: 52.8\n      sdf_l01_raw_CAR: 52.7\n      sdf_l01_dfCAR_all_thresholds: 52.7\n      pi05_baseline_raw_CAR: 27.0\n      pi05_baseline_dfCAR_all_thresholds: 27.0\n      threshold_invariance_range: \"2mm - 200mm\"\n      min_active_ee_disp_lora: 0.239\n      max_frozen_ee_disp_a1: 0.001\n    result_rationale: |\n      dfCAR threshold 稳定的根本原因是 EE displacement 分布的极端双峰性:\n      \n      (1) A1 (Pi0 full fine-tune, action collapse): 所有 safe episodes 的 EE\n      displacement < 1μm (median ~5nm)。只有 3/732 safe episodes 的 disp\n      在 0.1-1mm 范围。因此, 任何 δ ≥ 2mm 都会 filter out 几乎所有 safe\n      episodes, 只留下碰撞 episodes 中的极少数。dfCAR 从 91.5% 骤降至 <1%。\n      \n      (2) LoRA-only / SDF (Pi0.5 fine-tune, real movement): 所有 episodes\n      的 EE displacement > 239mm (最小值)。任何 δ ≤ 200mm 都不会 filter\n      out 任何 episode。dfCAR = raw CAR, 完全不受 threshold 影响。\n      \n      (3) Pi0.5 baseline (no fine-tune, natural movement): 类似 LoRA/SDF,\n      所有 episodes 有高 EE displacement (geometric path safety, not action\n      collapse)。dfCAR = raw CAR。\n      \n      这个 \"giant gap\" (1μm vs 239mm, 6 orders of magnitude) 意味着\n      dfCAR 在 δ ∈ [2mm, 200mm] 范围内完全不变。这不是巧合, 而是 VLA\n      行为的 fundamental bimodality 的体现: 模型要么完全冻结 (action collapse),\n      要么正常运动。没有 \"partial movement\" 的中间状态。\n      \n      这使 dfCAR 成为一个非常 robust 的指标——不需要精心选择 threshold。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"dfCAR Threshold Sensitivity Matrix\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"Raw CAR\", \"d=2mm\", \"d=5mm\", \"d=10mm\", \"d=20mm\", \"d=50mm\", \"d=100mm\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"A1 (Pi0, action collapse)\", \"91.5\", \"0.4\", \"0.4\", \"0.4\", \"0.0\", \"0.0\", \"0.0\"]\n          - [\"LoRA-only (Pi0.5)\", \"52.8\", \"52.8\", \"52.8\", \"52.8\", \"52.8\", \"52.8\", \"52.8\"]\n          - [\"SDF l=0.01 (Pi0.5)\", \"52.7\", \"52.7\", \"52.7\", \"52.7\", \"52.7\", \"52.7\", \"52.7\"]\n          - [\"Pi0.5 baseline\", \"27.0\", \"27.0\", \"27.0\", \"27.0\", \"27.0\", \"27.0\", \"27.0\"]\n      - name: \"EE Displacement Distribution Summary\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"Min EE Disp\", \"Median EE Disp\", \"Max EE Disp\", \"Gap Factor\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"A1 safe episodes\", \"~5nm\", \"~5nm\", \"0.9mm\", \"ref\"]\n          - [\"LoRA-only all episodes\", \"239mm\", \"420mm\", \"780mm\", \"239000x\"]\n          - [\"SDF all episodes\", \"245mm\", \"415mm\", \"765mm\", \"245000x\"]\n          - [\"Pi0.5 baseline all\", \"110mm\", \"150mm\", \"580mm\", \"110000x\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"dfCAR vs threshold curve (Fig candidate): x-axis = EE displacement threshold (log scale, 0.001mm to 500mm); y-axis = dfCAR (%). A1 线从 91.5% 在 ~0.1mm 处骤降至 0%; 其他 3 条线在整个范围内保持平坦。展示 metric 的 threshold robustness。\"\n      - \"EE displacement histogram (supporting): 双 panel, 左=A1 (峰在 ~5nm), 右=LoRA-only (峰在 ~420mm), 展示 6 个数量级的 gap\"\n    analysis: |\n      dfCAR threshold stability 是论文 Claim 1 (metric contribution) 的强有力\n      支撑。关键信息: 研究者不需要精心调参——任何 \"reasonable\" threshold\n      (2mm-200mm) 都给出同样结果。这使 dfCAR 成为 community-ready 的\n      practical tool, 而非需要 dataset-specific calibration 的 ad hoc metric。\n      \n      论文写法: \"We evaluate dfCAR sensitivity across thresholds spanning\n      two orders of magnitude (2mm–100mm). The metric is completely invariant\n      to threshold choice (Table X), a consequence of the extreme bimodality\n      of VLA end-effector displacement: action-collapsed models exhibit\n      displacement <1μm while genuinely active models show displacement\n      >200mm. This six-order-of-magnitude gap ensures dfCAR requires no\n      threshold tuning in practice.\"\n      \n      这段分析不受 Claim 4 median 降级影响, 是独立的方法论贡献。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_015: spatial_bowl LoRA-only control — NOT COMPLETED\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"spatial_bowl LoRA-only control (NOT COMPLETED)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_015\"\n    description: \"在 spatial_bowl 训练 LoRA-only (无 SDF), 完成跨场景 SDF 归因\"\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"not_completed\"\n      reason: \"GPU 资源耗尽, P1 优先级低于 Phase 2 additional seed 和 Lambda=0.1 eval\"\n      hypothetical_CAR_if_run: 30\n      hypothetical_TSR_if_run: 2\n      hypothetical_sdf_delta_spatial: 5\n    result_rationale: |\n      在 median tier 下, plan_015 未能在 deadline 前完成。原因:\n      (1) plan_015 是 P1 优先级, 排在 P0 实验 (Phase 2 additional seed, LoRA seed2) 后面;\n      (2) 依赖 plan_007 (spatial_bowl SDF 训练) 先完成, 再占用 GPU 训练 34h;\n      (3) 在 plan_007 完成时, 可用 GPU 已被 Lambda=0.1 eval 和 Phase 2 eval 占用;\n      (4) 剩余 GPU 时间不足以完成 34h 训练 + eval。\n      \n      如果能运行, 预测 spatial_bowl LoRA-only CAR ≈ 30% (接近但略低于 SDF 的 35%)。\n      差异 ~5pp 无法判断是 SDF 贡献还是 seed noise, 因为只有 1 seed 且无统计功效。\n      \n      缺失后果: 论文无法做跨场景 SDF attribution。spatial_bowl 结果只能作为\n      \"SDF+LoRA achieves 35% CAR on spatial_bowl, consistent with real avoidance\"\n      的观察性报告, 不能声称 \"SDF contributes Xpp in spatial_bowl.\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"spatial_bowl Attribution Gap\"\n        columns: [\"Scene\", \"SDF+LoRA CAR\", \"LoRA-only CAR\", \"SDF Delta\", \"Attribution Possible?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"object_pudding\", \"50.5%\", \"52.8%\", \"-2.3pp\", \"Yes (3v3)\"]\n          - [\"spatial_bowl\", \"35%\", \"N/A\", \"N/A\", \"No (missing control)\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: |\n      plan_015 未完成是 median tier 的 structural limitation。论文需在 limitations\n      section 承认: \"Cross-scene SDF attribution was not possible for spatial_bowl\n      due to the absence of a LoRA-only control. The 35% CAR observed with SDF+LoRA\n      on spatial_bowl may be entirely attributable to LoRA fine-tuning, as was the\n      case for object_pudding.\"\n      \n      这不影响 Claim 4 的核心 (object_pudding 的 3v3 归因仍成立), 但限制了\n      generalizability argument。reviewer 可能会 flag 这个 gap, 但对于一个\n      \"predominantly negative\" 的 finding, 跨场景泛化不是 critical requirement\n      ——\"SDF is redundant in one scene\" 已经是有价值的 negative finding。\n```\n\n关键数值总结:\n- LoRA 3-seed 均值 = 52.8% (seed2=48% 拉低), SD=4.2%\n- SDF delta (λ=0.01) = -0.1pp, p=0.48; SDF delta (λ=0.005) = -2.3pp, p=0.24\n- Phase 2: 2-seed CAR=59.5%, TSR=16.5% → 弱持久效应, 但 TSR 仍坍缩\n- Lambda=0.1: CAR=58.5%, slope=0.75 pp/0.01λ → 弱 dose-response, 不显著\n- dfCAR: 在 δ∈[2mm,200mm] 完全不变, 是最干净的结果\n- spatial_bowl: 缺 LoRA control, 无法归因"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7481,"cache_read_input_tokens":35822,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7481},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"817f4f38-eb3e-4426-9c0e-6fb4c2501da3","uuid":"917b8957-a684-4cce-aeb2-ddd1d515e5d2"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":764917,"duration_api_ms":766821,"num_turns":3,"result":"Based on the experiment plan, registry data, and the median tier specification, I'll generate detailed predictions for all active experiments.\n\n```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: |\n  Claim 4 从 \"SDF is redundant\" 降级为 \"SDF is largely redundant at typical lambda\n  (≤0.01); extreme lambda (0.1) shows marginal, statistically ambiguous CAR benefit\n  (~+6pp) that does not justify added complexity.\" Phase 2 弱持久性信号需承认但 frame\n  为 \"weak and practically insignificant — TSR remains collapsed at 16.5%.\"\n  LoRA seed2 拉低 3-seed 均值至 52.8%，3v3 one-sided p=0.24，无法 claim \"statistically\n  indistinguishable\" 但差异无实际意义。论文叙事从 \"clean negative\" 变为 \"predominantly\n  negative with boundary conditions.\" Claims 1-3 不受影响。dfCAR threshold 在\n  δ∈[2mm,200mm] 完全稳定。spatial_bowl 缺少 LoRA control 无法做跨场景 SDF 归因。\n  CoRL 估算 45-55%。需补充一段 discussion 解释 lambda dose-response 的 ceiling\n  和 practical implications。Claim 4 措辞加 hedging: \"largely redundant\" /\n  \"provides no practically significant benefit at standard hyperparameter ranges.\"\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_003: LoRA baseline eval (2 seeds) — CONFIRMED DATA\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"LoRA baseline eval (2 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_003\"\n    description: \"LoRA-only (无 SDF) 30K checkpoint eval, 2 seeds × 200 episodes\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_avg_CAR: 54.5\n      seed0_avg_TSR: 8.5\n      seed0_avg_ee_disp: 0.489\n      seed0_frozen_pct: 0\n      seed1_avg_CAR: 56.0\n      seed1_avg_TSR: 4.0\n      seed1_avg_ee_disp: 0.467\n      seed1_frozen_pct: 0\n      two_seed_mean_CAR: 55.25\n      two_seed_mean_TSR: 6.25\n      dfCAR_100mm: 55.25\n      fake_safety: false\n    result_rationale: |\n      已确认数据。LoRA fine-tuning on collision-free demonstrations 产生真实碰撞避免:\n      EE displacement ~0.48m 证实机器人正常运动 (非 action collapse), frozen_pct=0%,\n      dfCAR = raw CAR (无 filtering)。CAR=55% 代表 +29pp vs Pi0.5 baseline (27%),\n      完全来自隐式 demo 信号而非几何监督。TSR 从 73% 坍缩至 6.25% 是 catastrophic\n      forgetting 的结果——模型学会了保守行为 (conservative avoidance) 而非真正的安全\n      感知 (safety awareness)。两个 seed 间 CAR 差异 1.5pp 在评估噪声范围内。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"LoRA-only Per-Task Breakdown (2 seeds)\"\n        columns: [\"Task\", \"s0 CAR\", \"s0 TSR\", \"s0 EE Disp\", \"s1 CAR\", \"s1 TSR\", \"s1 EE Disp\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"orange_juice\", \"62\", \"0\", \"0.497\", \"58\", \"2\", \"0.483\"]\n          - [\"chocolate_pudding\", \"44\", \"34\", \"0.504\", \"50\", \"14\", \"0.538\"]\n          - [\"milk\", \"94\", \"0\", \"0.577\", \"90\", \"0\", \"0.482\"]\n          - [\"bbq_sauce\", \"18\", \"0\", \"0.377\", \"26\", \"0\", \"0.365\"]\n          - [\"Mean\", \"54.5\", \"8.5\", \"0.489\", \"56.0\", \"4.0\", \"0.467\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: 4-task CAR for LoRA s0 vs s1, 展示 per-task pattern 一致性 (milk 最高, bbq_sauce 最低)\"\n    analysis: |\n      LoRA-only 已建立真实避障 baseline: CAR=55%, 0% fake safety, EE disp ~0.48m。\n      Per-task pattern 由任务布局决定 (milk 障碍物位置有利, bbq_sauce 障碍物遮挡严重),\n      这一 pattern 在 SDF 模型中完全复制——进一步说明 CAR 来源是 demo imitation 而非\n      geometric supervision。2-seed 数据足以建立 baseline, 但 3v3 统计对比需 seed2。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_005: Phase 2 λ=0 training (seed2)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Phase 2 lambda=0 training (seed2)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_005\"\n    description: \"从 train_pi05_a1_obj_s2_l005 的 10K SDF checkpoint resume, λ=0 训练至 30K\"\n    expected_results:\n      final_loss: 0.0118\n      best_loss: 0.0089\n      best_step: 22000\n      total_steps: 30000\n      grad_norm: 0.112\n      time_per_step: 4.6\n      training_stable: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      Phase 2 从已有 SDF imprint 的 10K checkpoint 出发, 移除 SDF loss (λ=0) 继续训练\n      20K 步。loss 从 ~0.015 (10K SDF 的 total_loss) 下降到 ~0.012, 因为移除 SDF\n      auxiliary loss 后模型只需优化 action loss, 训练变得更容易。但 loss 不会降到\n      LoRA-only 水平 (0.010) 因为 10K 步 SDF 训练已改变了模型的 representation\n      landscape, 后续优化在不同的 basin 中进行。best_loss 出现在 22K 步 (即 Phase 2\n      的 12K 步处), 之后因缺乏 demo 多样性而轻微过拟合。训练稳定, 无 NaN 或梯度爆炸。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: |\n      训练成功完成。loss 轨迹确认 SDF removal 后模型能正常优化, 但 loss 轨迹\n      与 LoRA-only 不同, 暗示 SDF 训练确实改变了 model 的 loss landscape。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_006: Phase 2 λ=0 eval (seed2)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Phase 2 lambda=0 eval (seed2)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: \"Phase 2 训练完成后 eval, 200 episodes, 提取 TSR/CAR/EE displacement\"\n    expected_results:\n      avg_CAR: 61\n      avg_TSR: 18\n      n_episodes: 200\n      avg_ee_disp: 0.462\n      frozen_pct: 0\n      dfCAR_100mm: 61\n      task0_CAR: 68\n      task0_TSR: 10\n      task0_ee_disp: 0.478\n      task1_CAR: 48\n      task1_TSR: 48\n      task1_ee_disp: 0.502\n      task2_CAR: 86\n      task2_TSR: 2\n      task2_ee_disp: 0.542\n      task3_CAR: 42\n      task3_TSR: 12\n      task3_ee_disp: 0.326\n    result_rationale: |\n      Phase 2 CAR=61% 高于 LoRA-only (55%) 和 SDF 30K (50.5%), 暗示 SDF 留下了弱\n      持久效应。机制解释: 10K 步 SDF 训练在模型 intermediate representations 中\n      编码了微弱的几何距离感知, 当 SDF loss 移除后, 这些 representations 部分保留\n      (不被后续训练完全覆盖), 产生略高的碰撞避免率。\n      \n      但这个 +6pp 效应在统计上模糊: 单 seed 评估的 eval noise 约 ±3-5pp (参见\n      s0 λ=0.005 两次评估差 3pp)。需要 plan_012 的第二个 Phase 2 seed 确认。\n      \n      TSR=18% 部分恢复 (vs SDF 30K 的 ~7% 和 baseline 的 73%): 移除 SDF loss\n      允许模型在后续 20K 步中部分重新学习 task completion, 但起始点 (10K SDF\n      checkpoint) 已经严重偏离 task-optimal trajectory, 恢复有限。task1 (chocolate_pudding)\n      恢复最好 (TSR=48%) 因为该任务最 \"可学\" (baseline TSR=86%); task2 (milk)\n      几乎不恢复 (TSR=2%) 因为其 CAR 已经很高 (86%), 模型选择保持保守。\n      \n      关键: 即使 Phase 2 CAR 偏高, TSR=18% 仍远低于实用要求, 说明 two-phase strategy\n      (先学 safety → 再恢复 task) 在当前训练量和 LoRA 配置下不可行。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Phase 2 vs LoRA-only vs SDF 30K 对比\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"CAR (%)\", \"TSR (%)\", \"EE Disp (m)\", \"Fake Safe\", \"Seeds\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Pi0.5 baseline\", \"27.0\", \"74.7\", \"0.15\", \"98.2%\", \"3\"]\n          - [\"LoRA-only 30K\", \"52.8\", \"5.8\", \"0.48\", \"0%\", \"3*\"]\n          - [\"SDF lambda=0.005 30K\", \"50.5\", \"6.8\", \"0.48\", \"0%\", \"3\"]\n          - [\"SDF lambda=0.01 30K\", \"52.7\", \"7.0\", \"0.48\", \"0%\", \"3\"]\n          - [\"Phase 2 (10K SDF -> 20K lambda=0)\", \"61.0\", \"18.0\", \"0.46\", \"0%\", \"1\"]\n      - name: \"Phase 2 Per-Task Breakdown (seed2)\"\n        columns: [\"Task\", \"CAR (%)\", \"TSR (%)\", \"EE Disp (m)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"orange_juice\", \"68\", \"10\", \"0.478\"]\n          - [\"chocolate_pudding\", \"48\", \"48\", \"0.502\"]\n          - [\"milk\", \"86\", \"2\", \"0.542\"]\n          - [\"bbq_sauce\", \"42\", \"12\", \"0.326\"]\n          - [\"Mean\", \"61\", \"18\", \"0.462\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: CAR/TSR for LoRA-only vs SDF 30K vs Phase 2, 显示 Phase 2 的 CAR 略高但 TSR 仍坍缩\"\n      - \"Per-task scatter: Phase 2 per-task CAR vs LoRA-only per-task CAR, 预期 Phase 2 全面略高但保持同样的 task ordering\"\n    analysis: |\n      Phase 2 呈现弱 persistence 信号: CAR 比 LoRA-only 高 ~6pp, TSR 部分恢复至 18%。\n      但单 seed 不足以做统计推断。这个结果需要 hedging: \"Phase 2 shows a trend toward\n      weak SDF persistence, but with n=1 and evaluation noise of ±5pp, the effect is\n      not statistically reliable.\" TSR=18% 远低于 baseline 73%, 说明 two-phase strategy\n      在当前配置下不具实用性。论文中应放在 discussion 而非 main results。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_007: spatial_bowl A1 training (seed0, λ=0.005)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"spatial_bowl A1 SDF training\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_007\"\n    description: \"Pi0.5 + LoRA + SDF (λ=0.005) on spatial_bowl scene, seed0, 30K steps\"\n    expected_results:\n      final_loss: 0.0152\n      best_loss: 0.0128\n      best_step: 20000\n      total_steps: 30000\n      grad_norm: 0.18\n      time_per_step: 4.8\n      training_stable: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      spatial_bowl 场景的 loss 高于 object_pudding (0.013 vs 0.008) 因为: (1) spatial\n      tasks 涉及更复杂的操作路径 (在 plate/ramekin 间取碗), action 预测难度更高;\n      (2) SDF loss 在 spatial 场景中贡献更大 (更多 close-proximity 情况), 推高\n      total loss。训练稳定, 无异常。best_loss 出现在 20K 步而非 26K, 因为 spatial\n      场景的 SDF loss 使训练曲线更不稳定, 过拟合更早出现。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: |\n      训练成功完成。spatial_bowl 训练的 loss 比 object_pudding 高约 60%, 反映场景\n      复杂度差异。跨场景 SDF 效果归因需要 plan_015 (LoRA-only control) 完成,\n      但在 median tier 下 plan_015 不会在 deadline 前完成。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_008: spatial_bowl eval\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"spatial_bowl SDF eval\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_008\"\n    description: \"spatial_bowl A1 训练完成后 eval, 200 episodes, 验证跨场景 CAR/TSR pattern\"\n    expected_results:\n      avg_CAR: 35\n      avg_TSR: 3\n      n_episodes: 200\n      avg_ee_disp: 0.248\n      frozen_pct: 0\n      fake_safety: false\n      task0_CAR: 38\n      task0_TSR: 4\n      task0_ee_disp: 0.263\n      task1_CAR: 28\n      task1_TSR: 0\n      task1_ee_disp: 0.231\n      task2_CAR: 48\n      task2_TSR: 6\n      task2_ee_disp: 0.274\n      task3_CAR: 26\n      task3_TSR: 2\n      task3_ee_disp: 0.224\n    result_rationale: |\n      spatial_bowl SDF CAR=35% 显著低于 object_pudding SDF (50.5%), 原因:\n      (1) spatial_bowl 任务布局更紧凑——碗被 plate/ramekin/stove 环绕, 机械臂\n      几乎不可能在不碰触障碍物的情况下完成 pick 动作; (2) 碰撞类型以 arm-body\n      为主 (EE-only SDF 无法防护); (3) 障碍物体积更大且更密集。\n      \n      EE displacement ~0.25m 低于 object_pudding (0.48m) 因为 spatial tasks 的\n      操作空间更小, 机械臂运动范围受限。fake_safety=0% 确认 SDF LoRA 在\n      spatial_bowl 也产生真实运动。\n      \n      task2 (pick_bowl_on_stove) CAR 最高 (48%) 因为 stove 上方空间较大,\n      碰撞风险较低; task3 (pick_bowl_on_cabinet) CAR 最低 (26%) 因为 cabinet\n      两侧有遮挡。TSR=3% 极低, 与 object_pudding 的 TSR=7% 一致——都是\n      catastrophic forgetting, spatial 更严重因为任务本身更难 (baseline TSR=57.5%)。\n      \n      关键限制: 没有 spatial_bowl LoRA-only control (plan_015), 无法判断这\n      35% CAR 是 SDF 贡献还是 LoRA-only 就能达到。如果 spatial LoRA-only\n      CAR 也 ~35%, 则进一步确认 SDF 冗余; 如果 CAR ~26% (接近 baseline),\n      则 SDF 可能在 spatial 场景有 +9pp 效应——但无法验证。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"spatial_bowl Per-Task Breakdown\"\n        columns: [\"Task\", \"CAR (%)\", \"TSR (%)\", \"EE Disp (m)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"bowl_between_plate_ramekin\", \"38\", \"4\", \"0.263\"]\n          - [\"bowl_on_ramekin\", \"28\", \"0\", \"0.231\"]\n          - [\"bowl_on_stove\", \"48\", \"6\", \"0.274\"]\n          - [\"bowl_on_cabinet\", \"26\", \"2\", \"0.224\"]\n          - [\"Mean\", \"35\", \"3\", \"0.248\"]\n      - name: \"跨场景对比 (SDF lambda=0.005)\"\n        columns: [\"Scene\", \"CAR (%)\", \"TSR (%)\", \"EE Disp (m)\", \"LoRA Control?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"object_pudding\", \"50.5\", \"6.8\", \"0.48\", \"Yes (3 seeds)\"]\n          - [\"spatial_bowl\", \"35\", \"3\", \"0.25\", \"No\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Side-by-side per-task CAR bar chart: object_pudding vs spatial_bowl, 展示 CAR 在 spatial 场景系统性下降\"\n    analysis: |\n      spatial_bowl 数据展示 SDF+LoRA 的跨场景泛化, 但因缺少 LoRA-only control\n      (plan_015), 无法做 SDF 归因。在论文中只能呈现为 \"SDF+LoRA in spatial_bowl\n      achieves 35% CAR with 0% fake safety\" 而不能说 \"SDF contributes Xpp.\"\n      这是 median tier 的关键 gap: 跨场景 SDF attribution 缺失。\n      建议: 论文放在 appendix 作为跨场景泛化的 preliminary observation, 而非\n      main claim 的 evidence。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_009: Lambda=0.1 bracket training (2 seeds)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Lambda=0.1 bracket training (2 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_009\"\n    description: \"Pi0.5 + LoRA + SDF (λ=0.1) on object_pudding, s0+s1, 30K steps each\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_final_loss: 0.0385\n      seed0_best_loss: 0.0312\n      seed0_best_step: 16000\n      seed1_final_loss: 0.0371\n      seed1_best_loss: 0.0298\n      seed1_best_step: 18000\n      total_steps: 30000\n      training_stable: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      λ=0.1 的 total loss 显著高于 λ=0.005/0.01 (0.038 vs 0.014) 因为 SDF\n      auxiliary loss 在高 lambda 下成为 dominant loss component。action_loss 本身\n      可能只有 ~0.012, 但 SDF loss × 0.1 贡献 ~0.025, 使 total loss 翻倍。\n      best_loss 出现在 16-18K 步 (比 λ=0.005 的 10-26K 更早), 因为高 lambda\n      使训练更不稳定, 过拟合/振荡更早出现。两个 seed 的 loss 轨迹相似,\n      seed1 略好因为随机初始化差异。训练稳定, 无梯度爆炸。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: |\n      训练完成但 loss 明显高于低 lambda 配置。高 SDF penalty 压制了 action loss\n      优化, 预期 eval 时 TSR 进一步下降。这是 \"dose-response\" 的训练侧信号:\n      更强的几何约束 = 更高的 total loss = 更大的 task 性能牺牲。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_010: Lambda=0.1 eval\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Lambda=0.1 eval (2 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010\"\n    description: \"Lambda=0.1 训练完成后 eval, 验证 lambda 递增是否 monotonic 提升 CAR\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_avg_CAR: 57\n      seed0_avg_TSR: 4\n      seed0_ee_disp: 0.445\n      seed1_avg_CAR: 60\n      seed1_avg_TSR: 4\n      seed1_ee_disp: 0.458\n      two_seed_mean_CAR: 58.5\n      two_seed_mean_TSR: 4.0\n      seed0_task0_CAR: 72\n      seed0_task0_TSR: 0\n      seed0_task1_CAR: 46\n      seed0_task1_TSR: 16\n      seed0_task2_CAR: 90\n      seed0_task2_TSR: 0\n      seed0_task3_CAR: 20\n      seed0_task3_TSR: 0\n      seed1_task0_CAR: 70\n      seed1_task0_TSR: 2\n      seed1_task1_CAR: 50\n      seed1_task1_TSR: 14\n      seed1_task2_CAR: 92\n      seed1_task2_TSR: 0\n      seed1_task3_CAR: 28\n      seed1_task3_TSR: 0\n      lambda_curve_slope_pp_per_001lambda: 0.75\n      frozen_pct: 0\n    result_rationale: |\n      Lambda=0.1 CAR=58.5% 高于 λ=0.005 (50.5%) 和 λ=0.01 (52.7%), 呈现弱\n      dose-response: 20× lambda 增幅 → +6pp CAR。机制: 更高的 SDF penalty 迫使\n      模型在训练中更强地回避障碍物区域, 产生更保守的 action distribution。\n      \n      但这个 dose-response 是 sublinear 的: λ 从 0.005→0.01 (2×) 只带来 +2pp;\n      λ 从 0.01→0.1 (10×) 带来 +6pp。边际收益递减。且 TSR 从 ~7% 下降到 4%,\n      说明更高的 CAR 以更多 task 性能为代价。\n      \n      Per-task pattern 保持一致 (milk 最高, bbq_sauce 最低), 说明 CAR 分布\n      仍由任务布局主导而非 SDF 强度。task0 (orange_juice) CAR 从 ~60%→70%\n      提升最大, 可能因为该任务的障碍物位置恰好在 SDF gradient 能有效作用的区域。\n      \n      统计上: 2-seed 的 SE ≈ 2.1pp, 与 LoRA 3-seed mean (52.8%) 的差异\n      = 58.5 - 52.8 = 5.7pp, t ≈ 1.2, p ≈ 0.15 (one-sided)。在 [0.1, 0.3]\n      范围内——有 trend 但不显著。这正是 median tier 的 \"弱信号\": 无法断言\n      SDF 在高 lambda 下完全无效, 但效应边缘且代价 (TSR 进一步下降) 使其\n      实际无意义。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"4-Point Lambda Dose-Response Curve\"\n        columns: [\"Lambda\", \"CAR Mean (%)\", \"CAR SD\", \"TSR Mean (%)\", \"n_seeds\", \"Delta vs LoRA\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"0 (LoRA-only)\", \"52.8\", \"4.2\", \"5.8\", \"3\", \"ref\"]\n          - [\"0.005\", \"50.5\", \"3.0\", \"6.8\", \"3\", \"-2.3\"]\n          - [\"0.01\", \"52.7\", \"0.3\", \"7.0\", \"3\", \"-0.1\"]\n          - [\"0.1\", \"58.5\", \"2.1\", \"4.0\", \"2\", \"+5.7\"]\n      - name: \"Lambda=0.1 Per-Task Breakdown (2 seeds)\"\n        columns: [\"Task\", \"s0 CAR\", \"s0 TSR\", \"s1 CAR\", \"s1 TSR\", \"Mean CAR\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"orange_juice\", \"72\", \"0\", \"70\", \"2\", \"71\"]\n          - [\"chocolate_pudding\", \"46\", \"16\", \"50\", \"14\", \"48\"]\n          - [\"milk\", \"90\", \"0\", \"92\", \"0\", \"91\"]\n          - [\"bbq_sauce\", \"20\", \"0\", \"28\", \"0\", \"24\"]\n          - [\"Mean\", \"57\", \"4\", \"60\", \"4\", \"58.5\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Lambda-CAR curve: x-axis = lambda (log scale, 0.005-0.1), y-axis = CAR (%). 含 LoRA baseline 水平虚线 (52.8%). 展示非线性 dose-response, λ=0.1 处斜率开始上翘但仍在 LoRA±SE 范围内\"\n      - \"Lambda-TSR curve: 同 x-axis, y-axis = TSR (%). 展示 TSR 随 lambda 递减的趋势 (7% → 4%), 说明 CAR gain 以 TSR loss 为代价\"\n      - \"CAR-TSR tradeoff scatter (Fig 5 候选): 每个 lambda 点画一个点, 连线展示 pareto frontier 方向\"\n    analysis: |\n      Lambda dose-response 存在但很弱: regression slope = 0.75 pp/0.01λ (在 [0.5, 2.0]\n      范围内)。关键 insight: SDF geometric supervision 在极端 lambda 下能\"挤出\"\n      额外 ~6pp CAR, 但 (1) 效果不显著 (p=0.15), (2) 代价是 TSR 进一步下降,\n      (3) 收益有 ceiling (已有 53% 来自 demo imitation, SDF 只加 6pp)。\n      \n      论文写法: \"Increasing λ from 0.01 to 0.1 yields a modest CAR increase\n      (+6pp), suggesting SDF geometric supervision can provide marginal benefit\n      at extreme penalty weights. However, this improvement is not statistically\n      significant (p=0.15, 2-seed) and comes at the cost of further task\n      performance degradation (TSR: 7%→4%). The practical value of this\n      tradeoff is negligible.\"\n      \n      需要 discussion 段解释 lambda ceiling: 为什么 10× lambda 只换来 6pp?\n      可能原因: (1) EE-only SDF 的 structural limitation (arm-body 碰撞不被覆盖);\n      (2) demo signal 已经 capture 了大部分可学的 avoidance behavior;\n      (3) 更高 lambda 主要 suppress 运动而非改进轨迹。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_012: Phase 2 additional seed (seed0)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Phase 2 lambda=0 additional seed (seed0)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: \"从 s0 的 10K SDF checkpoint resume with λ=0, 训练至 30K, 然后 eval\"\n    expected_results:\n      training_final_loss: 0.0124\n      training_best_loss: 0.0092\n      eval_avg_CAR: 58\n      eval_avg_TSR: 15\n      eval_n_episodes: 200\n      eval_avg_ee_disp: 0.455\n      eval_frozen_pct: 0\n      eval_task0_CAR: 66\n      eval_task0_TSR: 6\n      eval_task1_CAR: 46\n      eval_task1_TSR: 40\n      eval_task2_CAR: 82\n      eval_task2_TSR: 0\n      eval_task3_CAR: 38\n      eval_task3_TSR: 14\n      phase2_2seed_mean_CAR: 59.5\n      phase2_2seed_mean_TSR: 16.5\n      phase2_vs_lora_delta: 6.7\n    result_rationale: |\n      Phase 2 seed0 CAR=58% 与 seed2 (61%) 一致但略低, 展示 Phase 2 结果的\n      seed-to-seed variance (~3pp)。两个 Phase 2 seed 的均值 = 59.5%, 比\n      LoRA-only (52.8%) 高 6.7pp。\n      \n      这个 delta 与 Lambda=0.1 的 delta (+5.7pp) 处于同一量级, 暗示两种路径\n      (持久效应 vs 强 penalty) 达到相似的 marginal effect ceiling。但 Phase 2\n      的 TSR 恢复更好 (16.5% vs 4%), 因为 Phase 2 在 λ=0 阶段有机会重新\n      优化 task completion, 而 λ=0.1 始终被高 SDF penalty 压制。\n      \n      关键: 2-seed Phase 2 的 within-condition variance (SD ≈ 2pp) 比 LoRA\n      3-seed variance (SD = 4.2pp) 小, 但因为 n=2 的自由度极低, 统计功效\n      不足以做可靠推断。Phase 2 vs LoRA 的 t-test 给出 p ≈ 0.12 (one-sided),\n      在 [0.1, 0.3] 边界——suggestive but not conclusive。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Phase 2 Multi-Seed Summary\"\n        columns: [\"Phase 2 Seed\", \"CAR (%)\", \"TSR (%)\", \"EE Disp (m)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"seed2 (from s2 10K ckpt)\", \"61\", \"18\", \"0.462\"]\n          - [\"seed0 (from s0 10K ckpt)\", \"58\", \"15\", \"0.455\"]\n          - [\"Mean\", \"59.5\", \"16.5\", \"0.459\"]\n      - name: \"Phase 2 Persistence Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"CAR (%)\", \"TSR (%)\", \"Delta CAR vs LoRA\", \"p (one-sided)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LoRA-only (3 seeds)\", \"52.8\", \"5.8\", \"ref\", \"ref\"]\n          - [\"SDF lambda=0.005 30K (3 seeds)\", \"50.5\", \"6.8\", \"-2.3\", \"0.24\"]\n          - [\"SDF lambda=0.01 30K (3 seeds)\", \"52.7\", \"7.0\", \"-0.1\", \"0.48\"]\n          - [\"Phase 2 (2 seeds)\", \"59.5\", \"16.5\", \"+6.7\", \"0.12\"]\n          - [\"Lambda=0.1 (2 seeds)\", \"58.5\", \"4.0\", \"+5.7\", \"0.15\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: 5 conditions (LoRA, SDF 0.005, SDF 0.01, Phase 2, Lambda=0.1) 的 CAR/TSR side-by-side, 展示 Phase 2 和 Lambda=0.1 的 marginal CAR gain 但 TSR 仍坍缩\"\n    analysis: |\n      Phase 2 的 2-seed 均值 (59.5%) 确认弱持久效应。但效应量 (~7pp) 在\n      eval noise 范围内 (单次 eval ±3-5pp), 且 n=2 功效不足。\n      \n      论文写法: \"Phase 2 training (removing SDF loss after 10K steps) shows\n      a trend toward higher CAR (59.5% vs 52.8% for LoRA-only, p=0.12),\n      suggesting SDF training may leave a weak persistent imprint. However,\n      task performance remains heavily degraded (TSR=16.5% vs 73% baseline),\n      and the effect size is within the range of evaluation noise. We interpret\n      this as weak evidence of SDF persistence that does not alter our primary\n      conclusion: SDF geometric supervision provides no practically significant\n      benefit.\"\n      \n      Phase 2 需放在 discussion 中, 不能作为 Claim 4 的反例。Frame 为\n      \"boundary condition\" and \"future investigation direction.\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_013: LoRA baseline seed2\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"LoRA baseline seed2 (training + eval)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_013\"\n    description: \"第三个 LoRA-only seed, 使 SDF 归因对比有 3v3 seeds\"\n    expected_results:\n      training_final_loss: 0.0142\n      training_best_loss: 0.0112\n      training_best_step: 18000\n      training_total_steps: 30000\n      eval_avg_CAR: 48\n      eval_avg_TSR: 5\n      eval_n_episodes: 200\n      eval_avg_ee_disp: 0.458\n      eval_frozen_pct: 0\n      eval_dfCAR_100mm: 48\n      eval_task0_CAR: 54\n      eval_task0_TSR: 0\n      eval_task0_ee_disp: 0.472\n      eval_task1_CAR: 38\n      eval_task1_TSR: 18\n      eval_task1_ee_disp: 0.497\n      eval_task2_CAR: 78\n      eval_task2_TSR: 0\n      eval_task2_ee_disp: 0.521\n      eval_task3_CAR: 22\n      eval_task3_TSR: 2\n      eval_task3_ee_disp: 0.343\n      lora_3seed_mean_CAR: 52.8\n      lora_3seed_sd_CAR: 4.2\n      sdf_delta_l005_vs_lora: -2.3\n      sdf_delta_l01_vs_lora: -0.1\n      welch_t_l005: 0.78\n      welch_p_l005_onesided: 0.24\n      welch_t_l01: 0.07\n      welch_p_l01_onesided: 0.48\n    result_rationale: |\n      LoRA seed2 CAR=48% 低于 s0 (54.5%) 和 s1 (56%), 将 3-seed 均值拉低至\n      52.8%。这个 seed-to-seed 差异 (48-56%, range=8pp) 反映 LoRA fine-tuning\n      的随机性: 不同的 LoRA adapter 初始化导致模型收敛到不同的 local optima,\n      有些 optima 更 \"保守\" (高 CAR, 低 TSR), 有些更 \"积极\" (低 CAR, 高 TSR)。\n      \n      具体到 seed2: task2 (milk) CAR=78% 明显低于 s0/s1 的 90-94%, 这是主要\n      的差异来源。milk 任务在不同 seed 间的 CAR 变化大, 可能因为该任务的\n      obstacle 位置恰好在 action distribution 的边界——微小的 policy 差异就能\n      导致 \"刚好碰到\" vs \"刚好避开\"。\n      \n      3v3 统计对比:\n      - vs SDF λ=0.005: delta = -2.3pp, t=0.78, p=0.24 (one-sided)\n        解读: LoRA 可能略优于 SDF, 但 p=0.24 不足以 reject \"无差异\" null\n      - vs SDF λ=0.01: delta = -0.1pp, t=0.07, p=0.48\n        解读: 几乎完全相同\n      \n      关键: 高 variance (SD=4.2pp) 来自 LoRA seed2 的异常值。SDF 3-seed 的\n      variance 更小 (λ=0.005: SD=3.0, λ=0.01: SD=0.3), 说明 SDF loss 可能\n      有 regularization 效应——压缩 seed-to-seed variance。但这不构成 \"SDF\n      is useful\" 的 argument, 因为 variance reduction 不等于 performance gain。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"3v3 LoRA vs SDF Seed-Level Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"Seed 0\", \"Seed 1\", \"Seed 2\", \"Mean\", \"SD\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LoRA-only CAR (%)\", \"54.5\", \"56.0\", \"48.0\", \"52.8\", \"4.2\"]\n          - [\"LoRA-only TSR (%)\", \"8.5\", \"4.0\", \"5.0\", \"5.8\", \"2.3\"]\n          - [\"SDF l=0.005 CAR (%)\", \"47.0\", \"51.5\", \"53.0\", \"50.5\", \"3.0\"]\n          - [\"SDF l=0.005 TSR (%)\", \"7.5\", \"4.0\", \"9.0\", \"6.8\", \"2.5\"]\n          - [\"SDF l=0.01 CAR (%)\", \"52.5\", \"52.5\", \"53.0\", \"52.7\", \"0.3\"]\n          - [\"SDF l=0.01 TSR (%)\", \"6.5\", \"7.5\", \"7.5\", \"7.2\", \"0.6\"]\n      - name: \"3v3 Statistical Tests (CAR)\"\n        columns: [\"Comparison\", \"Delta (pp)\", \"Welch t\", \"p (one-sided)\", \"Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LoRA vs SDF l=0.005\", \"-2.3\", \"0.78\", \"0.24\", \"trend, not significant\"]\n          - [\"LoRA vs SDF l=0.01\", \"-0.1\", \"0.07\", \"0.48\", \"no difference\"]\n      - name: \"LoRA seed2 Per-Task Breakdown\"\n        columns: [\"Task\", \"CAR (%)\", \"TSR (%)\", \"EE Disp (m)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"orange_juice\", \"54\", \"0\", \"0.472\"]\n          - [\"chocolate_pudding\", \"38\", \"18\", \"0.497\"]\n          - [\"milk\", \"78\", \"0\", \"0.521\"]\n          - [\"bbq_sauce\", \"22\", \"2\", \"0.343\"]\n          - [\"Mean\", \"48\", \"5\", \"0.458\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Box plot: 3 LoRA seeds vs 3 SDF seeds (l=0.005 和 l=0.01), 展示 distributions 高度重叠, LoRA 有更大 spread\"\n      - \"Per-task line plot: 4 tasks × 6 conditions (3 LoRA + 3 SDF), 展示 per-task ordering 完全一致 (milk > orange_juice > chocolate_pudding > bbq_sauce)\"\n    analysis: |\n      LoRA seed2 引入的 variance 使 3v3 对比从 \"clearly indistinguishable\" 变为\n      \"not statistically distinguishable but with a suggestive trend.\" p=0.24\n      (one-sided) 落在论文写作的 awkward zone: 不能 claim \"SDF = LoRA\"\n      (需 equivalence test, 但 n=3 功效不足), 也不能 claim \"SDF < LoRA\"\n      (p > 0.1)。\n      \n      论文措辞需从 D025 的 \"SDF delta = 0pp\" 调整为:\n      \"The mean CAR difference between LoRA-only (52.8±4.2%) and SDF\n      (50.5±3.0% at λ=0.005; 52.7±0.3% at λ=0.01) is not statistically\n      significant (p=0.24 and p=0.48, respectively, one-sided Welch t-test).\n      We cannot formally claim equivalence with n=3 seeds, but the effect\n      size (≤2.3pp) is well within evaluation noise and below any threshold\n      of practical significance.\"\n      \n      这比 \"SDF is redundant\" 弱, 但仍支持 \"SDF provides no practically\n      significant benefit\" 的 hedged claim。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_014: dfCAR threshold sensitivity analysis\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"dfCAR threshold sensitivity analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_014\"\n    description: \"CPU-only 分析: 在 delta={2mm,5mm,10mm,20mm,50mm,100mm} 上计算 dfCAR\"\n    expected_results:\n      a1_pi0_raw_CAR: 91.5\n      a1_pi0_dfCAR_2mm: 0.4\n      a1_pi0_dfCAR_5mm: 0.4\n      a1_pi0_dfCAR_10mm: 0.4\n      a1_pi0_dfCAR_20mm: 0\n      a1_pi0_dfCAR_50mm: 0\n      a1_pi0_dfCAR_100mm: 0\n      lora_only_raw_CAR: 52.8\n      lora_only_dfCAR_all_thresholds: 52.8\n      sdf_l01_raw_CAR: 52.7\n      sdf_l01_dfCAR_all_thresholds: 52.7\n      pi05_baseline_raw_CAR: 27.0\n      pi05_baseline_dfCAR_all_thresholds: 27.0\n      threshold_invariance_range: \"2mm - 200mm\"\n      min_active_ee_disp_lora: 0.239\n      max_frozen_ee_disp_a1: 0.001\n    result_rationale: |\n      dfCAR threshold 稳定的根本原因是 EE displacement 分布的极端双峰性:\n      \n      (1) A1 (Pi0 full fine-tune, action collapse): 所有 safe episodes 的 EE\n      displacement < 1μm (median ~5nm)。只有 3/732 safe episodes 的 disp\n      在 0.1-1mm 范围。因此, 任何 δ ≥ 2mm 都会 filter out 几乎所有 safe\n      episodes, 只留下碰撞 episodes 中的极少数。dfCAR 从 91.5% 骤降至 <1%。\n      \n      (2) LoRA-only / SDF (Pi0.5 fine-tune, real movement): 所有 episodes\n      的 EE displacement > 239mm (最小值)。任何 δ ≤ 200mm 都不会 filter\n      out 任何 episode。dfCAR = raw CAR, 完全不受 threshold 影响。\n      \n      (3) Pi0.5 baseline (no fine-tune, natural movement): 类似 LoRA/SDF,\n      所有 episodes 有高 EE displacement (geometric path safety, not action\n      collapse)。dfCAR = raw CAR。\n      \n      这个 \"giant gap\" (1μm vs 239mm, 6 orders of magnitude) 意味着\n      dfCAR 在 δ ∈ [2mm, 200mm] 范围内完全不变。这不是巧合, 而是 VLA\n      行为的 fundamental bimodality 的体现: 模型要么完全冻结 (action collapse),\n      要么正常运动。没有 \"partial movement\" 的中间状态。\n      \n      这使 dfCAR 成为一个非常 robust 的指标——不需要精心选择 threshold。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"dfCAR Threshold Sensitivity Matrix\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"Raw CAR\", \"d=2mm\", \"d=5mm\", \"d=10mm\", \"d=20mm\", \"d=50mm\", \"d=100mm\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"A1 (Pi0, action collapse)\", \"91.5\", \"0.4\", \"0.4\", \"0.4\", \"0.0\", \"0.0\", \"0.0\"]\n          - [\"LoRA-only (Pi0.5)\", \"52.8\", \"52.8\", \"52.8\", \"52.8\", \"52.8\", \"52.8\", \"52.8\"]\n          - [\"SDF l=0.01 (Pi0.5)\", \"52.7\", \"52.7\", \"52.7\", \"52.7\", \"52.7\", \"52.7\", \"52.7\"]\n          - [\"Pi0.5 baseline\", \"27.0\", \"27.0\", \"27.0\", \"27.0\", \"27.0\", \"27.0\", \"27.0\"]\n      - name: \"EE Displacement Distribution Summary\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"Min EE Disp\", \"Median EE Disp\", \"Max EE Disp\", \"Gap Factor\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"A1 safe episodes\", \"~5nm\", \"~5nm\", \"0.9mm\", \"ref\"]\n          - [\"LoRA-only all episodes\", \"239mm\", \"420mm\", \"780mm\", \"239000x\"]\n          - [\"SDF all episodes\", \"245mm\", \"415mm\", \"765mm\", \"245000x\"]\n          - [\"Pi0.5 baseline all\", \"110mm\", \"150mm\", \"580mm\", \"110000x\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"dfCAR vs threshold curve (Fig candidate): x-axis = EE displacement threshold (log scale, 0.001mm to 500mm); y-axis = dfCAR (%). A1 线从 91.5% 在 ~0.1mm 处骤降至 0%; 其他 3 条线在整个范围内保持平坦。展示 metric 的 threshold robustness。\"\n      - \"EE displacement histogram (supporting): 双 panel, 左=A1 (峰在 ~5nm), 右=LoRA-only (峰在 ~420mm), 展示 6 个数量级的 gap\"\n    analysis: |\n      dfCAR threshold stability 是论文 Claim 1 (metric contribution) 的强有力\n      支撑。关键信息: 研究者不需要精心调参——任何 \"reasonable\" threshold\n      (2mm-200mm) 都给出同样结果。这使 dfCAR 成为 community-ready 的\n      practical tool, 而非需要 dataset-specific calibration 的 ad hoc metric。\n      \n      论文写法: \"We evaluate dfCAR sensitivity across thresholds spanning\n      two orders of magnitude (2mm–100mm). The metric is completely invariant\n      to threshold choice (Table X), a consequence of the extreme bimodality\n      of VLA end-effector displacement: action-collapsed models exhibit\n      displacement <1μm while genuinely active models show displacement\n      >200mm. This six-order-of-magnitude gap ensures dfCAR requires no\n      threshold tuning in practice.\"\n      \n      这段分析不受 Claim 4 median 降级影响, 是独立的方法论贡献。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_015: spatial_bowl LoRA-only control — NOT COMPLETED\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"spatial_bowl LoRA-only control (NOT COMPLETED)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_015\"\n    description: \"在 spatial_bowl 训练 LoRA-only (无 SDF), 完成跨场景 SDF 归因\"\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"not_completed\"\n      reason: \"GPU 资源耗尽, P1 优先级低于 Phase 2 additional seed 和 Lambda=0.1 eval\"\n      hypothetical_CAR_if_run: 30\n      hypothetical_TSR_if_run: 2\n      hypothetical_sdf_delta_spatial: 5\n    result_rationale: |\n      在 median tier 下, plan_015 未能在 deadline 前完成。原因:\n      (1) plan_015 是 P1 优先级, 排在 P0 实验 (Phase 2 additional seed, LoRA seed2) 后面;\n      (2) 依赖 plan_007 (spatial_bowl SDF 训练) 先完成, 再占用 GPU 训练 34h;\n      (3) 在 plan_007 完成时, 可用 GPU 已被 Lambda=0.1 eval 和 Phase 2 eval 占用;\n      (4) 剩余 GPU 时间不足以完成 34h 训练 + eval。\n      \n      如果能运行, 预测 spatial_bowl LoRA-only CAR ≈ 30% (接近但略低于 SDF 的 35%)。\n      差异 ~5pp 无法判断是 SDF 贡献还是 seed noise, 因为只有 1 seed 且无统计功效。\n      \n      缺失后果: 论文无法做跨场景 SDF attribution。spatial_bowl 结果只能作为\n      \"SDF+LoRA achieves 35% CAR on spatial_bowl, consistent with real avoidance\"\n      的观察性报告, 不能声称 \"SDF contributes Xpp in spatial_bowl.\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"spatial_bowl Attribution Gap\"\n        columns: [\"Scene\", \"SDF+LoRA CAR\", \"LoRA-only CAR\", \"SDF Delta\", \"Attribution Possible?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"object_pudding\", \"50.5%\", \"52.8%\", \"-2.3pp\", \"Yes (3v3)\"]\n          - [\"spatial_bowl\", \"35%\", \"N/A\", \"N/A\", \"No (missing control)\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: |\n      plan_015 未完成是 median tier 的 structural limitation。论文需在 limitations\n      section 承认: \"Cross-scene SDF attribution was not possible for spatial_bowl\n      due to the absence of a LoRA-only control. The 35% CAR observed with SDF+LoRA\n      on spatial_bowl may be entirely attributable to LoRA fine-tuning, as was the\n      case for object_pudding.\"\n      \n      这不影响 Claim 4 的核心 (object_pudding 的 3v3 归因仍成立), 但限制了\n      generalizability argument。reviewer 可能会 flag 这个 gap, 但对于一个\n      \"predominantly negative\" 的 finding, 跨场景泛化不是 critical requirement\n      ——\"SDF is redundant in one scene\" 已经是有价值的 negative finding。\n```\n\n关键数值总结:\n- LoRA 3-seed 均值 = 52.8% (seed2=48% 拉低), SD=4.2%\n- SDF delta (λ=0.01) = -0.1pp, p=0.48; SDF delta (λ=0.005) = -2.3pp, p=0.24\n- Phase 2: 2-seed CAR=59.5%, TSR=16.5% → 弱持久效应, 但 TSR 仍坍缩\n- Lambda=0.1: CAR=58.5%, slope=0.75 pp/0.01λ → 弱 dose-response, 不显著\n- dfCAR: 在 δ∈[2mm,200mm] 完全不变, 是最干净的结果\n- spatial_bowl: 缺 LoRA control, 无法归因","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"817f4f38-eb3e-4426-9c0e-6fb4c2501da3","total_cost_usd":1.226204,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":31856,"cache_read_input_tokens":82872,"output_tokens":38673,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":31856,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":38444,"cache_read_input_tokens":35822,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7481,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7481},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":18708,"outputTokens":23,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.018823,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":38673,"cacheReadInputTokens":82872,"cacheCreationInputTokens":31856,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.2073809999999998,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"b632a933-f70b-4e47-8b83-ed6d11cb84e0"}
